# Manual requests for the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client). The full, current list is in
# Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html (sign in there with Authorize).
#
# Run "Sign in" first: the requests below reuse its access token (valid 15 minutes; run it again, or
# "Refresh", when calls start answering 401). The refresh cookie is kept by the client between requests.
@host = http://localhost:8080
@email = admin@example.com
@password = change-me
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Sign in
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Who am I (and which teams can I see)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change the password (required after the first sign-in; returns a new token: sign in again to reuse it here)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"currentPassword": "{{password}}", "newPassword": "a-new-password-of-12+-characters"}

### Refresh: a new access token from the refresh cookie
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

### Sign out (ends this session and clears the cookie)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### Teams
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Engineers of one team, by name
GET {{host}}/api/v1/engineers?team=SRE&active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Newest alerts (paged)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Alerts filtered by engineer, severity and date, oldest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts?engineerId=1&severity=P1&start=2016-01-01&end=2016-12-31&sort=triggeredAt,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Paging history of one alert
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts/1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### On-call shifts
GET {{host}}/api/v1/oncall?start=2026-09-01&end=2026-09-30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Fairness (2016 data needs an explicit window; non-admins get their own team)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/fairness?start=2016-01-01&end=2016-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Burnout (admins and managers)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/burnout?days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Time of day
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/timeofday?days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### All scores for one engineer
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/engineers/1?days=90
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics: everything the page shows, for one team and month
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/snapshot?team=SRE&start=2026-09-01&end=2026-09-30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics: KPIs against the previous 30 days
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics: weekly alert counts by severity for 2016
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/alerts/timeseries?start=2016-01-01&end=2016-12-31&granularity=week
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Users (admins only)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users?role=MANAGER
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a manager of team 1 (the response has a one-time password)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "manager@example.com", "fullName": "Team Manager", "role": "MANAGER", "teamIds": [1]}

### Create an engineer login for engineer 1
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "engineer@example.com", "fullName": "On-call Engineer", "role": "ENGINEER", "engineerId": 1}

### Set the teams a manager can see
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"teamIds": [1, 2]}

### Reset a user's password (new one-time password, sessions ended)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit log: recent failed sign-ins (admins only)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/audit?action=LOGIN_FAILED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### PagerDuty incidents (live, not stored; admins only)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/incidents?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### PagerDuty users
GET {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sync incidents now
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Backfill a year of on-call shifts
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/sync/oncalls?days=365
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Resolve an incident as a PagerDuty user
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/resolve/INCIDENT_ID?email=engineer@example.com
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Webhook ping (unversioned path, no token; real events need a valid X-PagerDuty-Signature)
POST {{host}}/api/webhook/pagerduty
Content-Type: application/json

{"event": {"event_type": "pagey.ping"}}
